---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import SupportArticle from "../../components/infopages/SupportArticle.astro";
---
<BaseLayout>
  <SupportArticle path="/support/add-products" title="Ways to add a product" intro="There's more than one way to get your collection into BeautyMark. Pick whichever is quickest for the product in front of you.">

    <h2>Scan it with your camera</h2>
    <p> Got the product in your hand? Tap <strong>+</strong> and take a photo of its label. BeautyMark reads the label, finds the product, and fills in the brand, name, shade and a photo for you. <a href="/support/scan-a-product">How to scan a product</a>
    </p>

    <h2>Find it by name</h2>
    <p> Know what it's called? Type a few words of the brand or product, like "cerave moist", and pick it from a list of tens of thousands of products from Sephora, Ulta, Target and lots of brands' own shops. <a href="/support/find-a-product">How to find a product by name</a>
    </p>

    <h2>Share it from a store</h2>
    <p> Shopping (or wishlisting) on a store's website or app? Tap Share on the product page and choose BeautyMark, and it arrives filled in, photo and all. <a href="/support/add-from-a-store">How to add a product from a store</a>
    </p>

    <h2>Duplicate one you already have</h2>
    <p> Picked up the same product in another shade? Duplicate it and change just the shade. <a href="/support/duplicate-a-product">How to duplicate a product</a>
    </p>

    <h2>Not in our list?</h2>
    <p>You can always type a product in yourself. When you save one we didn't know, BeautyMark may offer to share it (just the words, never your photos) so it's in everyone's list after a future update. <a href="/support/find-a-product">More about sharing</a></p>

    <h2>What every product needs</h2>
    <p> To save a product, BeautyMark needs a <strong>brand</strong>, a <strong>product name</strong> and a <strong>photo</strong>. Everything else (category, shade, link, notes, dates) is up to you. With the free version you can keep up to 20 products; <a href="/#pricing">BeautyMark Pro</a> removes the limit.
    </p>
  </SupportArticle>
</BaseLayout>
